<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 52 — Health Checks & Actuator Hardening.
    health/        Status, HealthCheck, HealthGroup (worst-member aggregation, per-check timeout), CachedCheck
    availability/  Availability: liveness and readiness as the application's own state, like Spring Boot's
    shutdown/      GracefulShutdown: refuse readiness, drain, finish in-flight requests
    pg/            PgPing: a PostgreSQL SELECT 1 over the wire protocol, for the lab's database check
    resources/     application.yml (probe groups, separate management port, locked-down endpoints) and k8s/
                   (Deployment with startup, liveness and readiness probes and a preStop sleep; NetworkPolicy)
  verify/run.sh runs order-service on a real Kubernetes cluster (k3s 1.37) with PostgreSQL outside it: a database
  outage under three probe designs, slow startup, rolling restarts under load, heap dumps and the management port.
-->
